<title>SPAIN: Spain had June c/account deficit of 30.8 bln ptas.</title>
<headline>Spain had June c/account deficit of 30.8 bln ptas.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		 JUNE 96     MAY 96     JUNE 95</p>
<p>  C/A balance			   -30.8	 -9.5	   9.9</p>
<p>  Trade balance			-152.4     -196.8	-186.4</p>
<p>  Services				230.0	206.6	 224.9</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts		247.0	232.9	 244.8</p>
<p>  Other services			-17.0	-26.3	 -20.0</p>
<p>  Dividend income		    -137.5	-51.4	 -47.8</p>
<p>  Transfers				29.0	 32.0	  19.3</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		     145.6	 31.2	  82.9</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		    19.5	  2.4	 -36.0</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad	   3.9	-22.5	-256.0</p>
<p>  Foreign investment in Spain     245.7     -101.5	 475.5</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,deposits abroad   102.9	147.4	-109.5</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain   -284.7	387.6	-116.7</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves		-48.3     -408.6	 -29.2</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is negative 134.3 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
